<title>CHINA: LG wins $100 mln China LNG store contract.</title>
<headline>LG wins $100 mln China LNG store contract.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A unit of South Korea's LG Group has won a $100 million contract to design and build a liquefied natural gas (LNG) storage facility in southern China for Caltex Corp, the official Xinhua news agency said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Caltex is a 50-50 joint venture between Chevron Corp and Texaco Inc, both of the United States.  </p>
<p>Xinhua quoted LG Group as saying in a statement from Shanghai that group company LG Engineering Co won the contract over 13 rivals.</p>
<p>It said the contract calls for construction of two underground 100,000-cubic-metre facilities as well as an office centre in Shantou in China's southern province of Guangdong.</p>
<p>The facilities are scheduled to be operational in 1998.</p>
<p>Xinhua gave no further details.</p>
</text>
